    "Static configs work only for fixed, known targets.",
    "Static configs fail for ASG targets because instances and their IPs are created and removed dynamically.",
    "When ASG instances change, the static list becomes stale and misses new instances or keeps removed ones.",
    "EC2 service discovery in Prometheus YAML queries AWS to describe EC2 instances and automatically finds current targets.",
    "EC2 service discovery is driven by tags on the instances.",
    "You tag ASG instances and EC2 service discovery finds them by tag.",
    "Prometheus will start scraping metrics from instances as they start and stop, keeping the target list dynamic and up to date.",
    "By default, EC2 service discovery uses private IPs.",
    "You can change EC2 service discovery to use public IPs via relabeling rules.",
    "EC2 service discovery requires IAM permission for EC2 DescribeInstances exposed to the Prometheus host.",
    "This permission is typically provided by attaching a role to the EC2 instance running Prometheus.",
    "ASG instances are ephemeral.",
    "ASG IPs and instance counts change automatically with scaling.",
    "Static configs require fixed addresses and cannot track ASG changes.",
    "Static configs miss newly created instances and keep removed ones.",
    "EC2 service discovery is needed to dynamically discover and scrape the correct, current targets."
